    @section parse_if %if

    @par Parse Directive:
    <tt>%%if</tt> \em expression

    @par Command Line:
    n/a

    @par Parse Option Constant:
    n/a

    @par Description:
    Opens a conditionally-parsed block with boolean expression support. The expression can use the following operators:
    - \c defined(SYMBOL) - returns true if SYMBOL is defined
    - \c ! - logical NOT operator
    - \c && - logical AND operator
    - \c || - logical OR operator
    - \c () - parentheses for grouping

    @par Examples:
    @code{.py}
# Simple defined check
%if defined(DEBUG)
    printf("Debug mode\n");
%endif

# Boolean logic
%if defined(FEATURE_A) && !defined(LEGACY_MODE)
    printf("Feature A enabled\n");
%endif

# Complex expression
%if (defined(UNIX) || defined(LINUX)) && defined(HAS_NETWORK)
    printf("Unix with networking\n");
%endif
    @endcode

    @see @ref conditional_parsing

