    @section no-summarize %no-summarize

    @par Parse Directive:
    <tt>%%no-summarize</tt>

    @par Command Line:
    <tt>-</tt><tt>-set-parse-option=no-summarize</tt>

    @par Parse Option Constant:
    <tt>"no-summarize"</tt> (via @ref Qore::ParseOptions)

    @par Description:
    Disallows the \c summarize statement at parse time. When this option is set, any
    \c summarize statement triggers a parse error. The recommended rewrite is to
    iterate a plain @ref context "context" loop and perform grouping manually.

    This option is implied by @ref modern "%modern" and therefore applies to all
    \c .qr files and any program started with the \c -M command-line flag or the
    @ref Qore::PO_MODERN option constant.

    @note This is an extended parse option (bit 69). The Qore constant \c PO_NO_SUMMARIZE
    is defined as \c 0 for backward compatibility with the legacy 64-bit integer
    parse-option space; use the string name \c "no-summarize" with the @ref Qore::ParseOptions
    class when setting parse options programmatically.

